  "finding": "Current Dutch OER controls. Ordinary single-degree allocation totals 180 EC, with at least 6 EC genuinely open inside the 39 EC choice space. The optional astronomy minor and dual degree are separate. The combined 9 EC laboratory/data module supersedes earlier units; separate 3 EC PPD and portfolio are retained. Mandatory RADAr participation adds no credits. The current English catalogue lists introductory quantum mechanics and Linear Algebra A or NS as presumed knowledge for Quantum Mechanics 1. The ordinary first year includes Introduction to Quantum Mechanics and Linear Algebra NS. The dual-degree transition is not needed to establish this progression. Internship entry requires the full first year and 120 EC total, approval and registration; research is assessed through the report and symposium."
